# =============================================================================
# Customer-name list for tools/hooks/pre-commit - EXAMPLE
# =============================================================================
# Copy to ~/.config/ihw/customer_patterns (tools/hooks/install.sh does it) and
# put in the names of YOUR customers. The real list never goes into git - it
# would publish the very names it protects.
#
# Format, one entry per line:
#   <regex>          extended regex, case-insensitive  (host, domain, company)
#   cs:<regex>       extended regex, case-sensitive    (short upper-case codes)
#   allow:<string>   literal string removed before the check (false positive),
#                    or an exact IP address the private-IP check should accept
#   # comment / empty line
#
# Demo data of this repository (README "Demo Data") is allowed and must NOT be
# listed: orafusion01, pipperr.local, 10.10.10.0/24, FMWCDB / fmwpdb,
# fr_domain, repserver01, reportGPI, user gpi.
# =============================================================================

# customer company / project names
examplecorp
# host and domain names of the customer
srvexample0[0-9]
example-intra\.local
# customer network outside the private ranges (private ranges are checked anyway)
203\.0\.113\.
# short upper-case customer code - case-sensitive, word start
cs:\bEXC
# false positive: "exc" in "exception" is not the customer
allow:exception
